5	**Goal:** Turn item detail from an edit form into what the design specifies — a read-first view that shows how you actually wear a piece, with editing moved behind the `⋯` overflow.
6	
7	**Architecture:** The screen inverts. `page.tsx` loads the item plus its wear history and a deterministic "goes with" set; the read view renders stats, tag rows and the complementary row; the existing form moves wholesale into a sheet opened from `⋯`. "Goes with" reuses the generator's own scoring — no new algorithm, no AI call.
