22	## Decision required — read this before starting
23	
24	The design's primary CTA is **"Style an outfit with this"** (`:654`). That conflicts with Decision 5
25	(CLAUDE.md): looks are a daily drop, generated once per local day, and tapping an occasion reads stored
26	rows without calling the model. Styling around a chosen item is inherently on demand.
27	
28	**This plan assumes the cheap reading**, and Task 5 is written against it:
29	
30	> Tapping filters **today's already-stored looks** to those containing this item and opens the first
31	> match. If none contain it, the button offers *"Build a look around this"*, which runs a real
32	> generation and **consumes the regenerate quota** (`lib/outfits/quota.ts`).
33	
34	That keeps the free tier free, honours Decision 5, and gives the quota seam its first real consumer.
35	The alternative — an AI call on every tap — would make this button the largest per-user cost in the
36	product. **If you want that instead, change Task 5 before implementing it, not after.**
37	
38	Second assumption: **prices are GBP**, formatted with `Intl.NumberFormat("en-GB")`, because the design
39	prices Pro at `£5/mo` and shows `£3.28` cost-per-wear. A currency setting belongs to the Settings plan;
40	until it exists, one hard-coded currency beats a fake one.
